L001260	\section{Cryo-CMOS qubit controller}\label{cryo-cmos-qubit-controller}
L001261	
L001262	The cryo-CMOS qubit controller is a high-performance, mixed-signal system-on-chip fabricated in a commercial 130-nm RF CMOS technology.
L001263	Circuit designs are optimized at the transistor level for cryogenic performance.
L001264	The controller is designed to control an array of exchange-only silicon spin qubits from the 4~K stage of a commercial dilution refrigerator.
L001265	It generates all time-varying voltage signals required to perform tune-up, state preparation and measurement (SPAM), and qubit state manipulation.
L001266	The controller die contains 70 million transistors, measures 21 $\times$ 19~mm\textsuperscript{2}, and has 3054 C4-style pins arranged in a ground-signal/power-ground pattern with a minimum pad pitch of 250~$\mu$m.
L001267	
L001268	Figure~\ref{figS1}
L001269	depicts a photograph of a die with the main sections of the design annotated and
L001270	
L001271	\figref{figS2} shows a top-level block diagram of the controller.
L001272	
