L001481	
L001482	The cryo-controller requires one digital power supply and six analog power supplies from room temperature.
L001483	Power consumed by the digital architecture is dynamic power and is therefore a strong function of the operating frequency and the complexity of the program.
L001484	The analog gate driver layer power consumption is mostly static because the typical duty cycle for pulsed outputs during an experiment is \textless~10\%.
L001485	Empirical data suggests randomized benchmarking consumes more digital power that the other kinds of experiments discussed in this publication.
L001486	For an optimized single-sequencer, single-qubit RB experiment at 250~MHz, the chip consumes approximately 2.8~W.
L001487	A detailed power breakdown of this scenario is shown in \figref{figS10}.
L001488	It is estimated that power consumption would increase up to 3.5~W if all six sequencers were independently running randomized benchmarking.
L001489	
L001490	
L001491	The total power consumption is within the typically-available thermalization budget of the 4~K stage in commercial dilution refrigerators.
L001492	The controller features granular power control such that most digital assets and analog sub-circuits can be powered down when not in use.
L001493	Approaches to substantially reducing the power-per-qubit through architecture and scaling have been identified, but were not required for this work.
