L001495	\section{Superconducting interconnect}\label{superconducting-interconnect-sup}
L001496	
L001497	\subsection{Fabrication}\label{fabrication}
L001498	
L001499	The superconducting ribbon cables are fabricated on 150~mm silicon wafers using Nb for the superconducting layers and polyimide for the dielectric.
L001500	Polyimide layers serve as both low-K interlayer dielectric (ILD) and in providing structural support for the ribbon cable.
L001501	Three levels of Nb metal realize a lower ground plane, a signal layer, and an upper ground plane to create a fully-enclosed stripline environment.
L001502	Via trenches are formed between each signal trace, electrically connecting the upper and lower ground planes.
L001503	The resulting structure (\figref{figS11}) is a rectangular coaxial structure with micron-scale signal wires on a 15~$\mu$m pitch.
L001504	Pads are finished with Au to support assembly operations.
L001505	Typical cable designs are 6~cm long, approximately 1~cm wide, and implement 200 to 500 independent signal wires.
L001506	High-yielding wafer-scale processes are able to routinely realize devices with 100\% interconnect yield for these 6~cm\textsuperscript{2} devices.
