L001818	\section{Tune-up and calibration}\label{tune-up-and-calibration}
L001819	
L001820	Our Quiver control software includes a large suite of available measurements, analyses, and automated routines that enables users to efficiently tune-up, calibrate, and characterize the qubit device and controller with a high degree of flexibility.
L001821	
L001822	Due to material and fabrication non-uniformity, both within and between devices, device tune-up is exploratory and non-deterministic.
L001823	Figure \ref{figS20} shows an overview of the basic tune up workflow divided in to four phases.
L001824	Effective optimization within and between phases often requires iterative trial, evaluation, and adjustment.
L001825	Dead ends require returning to known-good checkpoints where alternative paths can subsequently be explored.
L001826	The software is designed to be flexible for users with loops, backtracking, conditional branching, and adaptive heuristics supported as first-class concepts.
L001827	In addition to providing all the components required to enable tune-up, we have begun capturing proven workflows that combine the components into automated routines such that tune-up can proceed with increasingly less human interaction.
