L002486	
L002487	We model voltage propagation through our entire analog signal chain assembly, consisting of a cryo-controller, various interconnect sub-assemblies and the qubit chip.
L002488	Voltage pulses are simulated in the time-domain using industry-standard SPICE simulation software.
L002489	ISI and XTK, driven by component design as well as unavoidable impedance mismatches, result in complex and unpredictable pulse reflections whose errors can only be fully-accounted via SPICE simulation of the full-scale, end-to-end interconnect of the integrated system.
L002490	Such a circuit model is constructed by chaining together a series of (sub)circuit multiconductor models corresponding to individual components of the assembly (\figref{figS35}).
L002491	These components span several orders of magnitude in physical size and embody a range of electrical complexity that merits the application of a unique modeling approach for each element in the end-to-end model.
L002492	We have developed methods for generating high-fidelity models based on cross-sectional 2D TEM analysis, 3D full-wave electromagnetic simulations as well as lumped element models where appropriate.
L002493	The end-to-end circuit model is used to generate the multi-input multi-output (MIMO) impulse response by performing a series of transient SPICE simulations, which is then convolved into sampled controller waveforms and mapped into the singlet-triplet exchange domain, to add the expected angle rotation errors to the ideal exchange sequence.
