L002775	In the distance-3 repetition code, we use pymatching \cite{s_higgott_sparse_2025} to construct a minimum-weight perfect matching decoder, assuming a uniform depolarizing error channel given the error rates of CNOTs, dynamic decoupling exchanges, etc.
L002776	In both metrics, the most dominant first-order noise contribution is the ersatz quasi-static miscalibration, followed by the nuclear magnetic noise term \(T_{2}^{*}\).
